      "hash": "bc47da663d101bfc1d4edcb3762f37fbe8fab3e931cfd460c69cb432b806d419"
    },
    {
      "id": "39827998d28149e06470a0fa0a9009c9e7ccd67b8c4b3262c8bca6337e58fa56",
      "text": "Copy page",
      "hash": "4104018941ae3ab016c117887a91b4f933f28e36c587b8983373fe9377ce34d7"
    },
    {
      "id": "65917135aeda8298beaa006f68e689c2a6612266696d702ca7fd4271e3122600",
      "text": "Share",
      "hash": "29887a5ff9846ccc23327565a07e17fa6dcaea6211f1898ae825f84ae38f4223"
    },
    {
      "id": "07145425123b1fb45fd95a16cc74dc2a059cde63d12fe5bc4fbacf53c4f9a36c",
      "text": "Next lesson",
      "hash": "d0ae2a13d8665949dd104a2fbdedcc8bca3e647a1e131d1ebaeb31c189a553b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "d620448277312c9b8e5ede21beb4c0f1e432c55fba56cd91c3c40fcbc133b8c3",
      "text": "On this page",
      "hash": "b5658fc8edda24f9c94eabac9e536e0a18e3055a8ca255f9d1b8f256ea02a6cc"
    },
    {
      "id": "60f619f100f542154d46f93cbe32d1790b606389b808dd9f1ad98d6f89032a55",
      "text": "Zod Schema",
      "hash": "64e027dcfb566284c657b69a5f48405d9f4a25c9b544326fd38522b1925bec3c"
    },
    {
      "id": "9bfcfc0c15367b0e4273db5baccf5963ec869085e5a824475535c85bfb57d9be",
      "text": "Passing The Schema To",
      "hash": "563346bf85a3a8ce18f85cce9dc3b16ea841a1be11ed3bfb3fa902735b0fc734"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf5cf55bcf69b5ac5d080d781dbe5eaeb6966c637571e72290bd5b55704da754",
      "text": "Up next",
      "hash": "e31da5b25f8b7324861e9aadaf5c503e7fd43e739fa3be17ebe63e999fb13df1"
    },
    {
      "id": "4f4400718fbdc87aca6a3edc08eeb94644649ab25c247b4f8b27fd692eecdb4a",
      "text": "So far we've looked at getting an LLM to return objects or enums (enumerated values) instead of just returning text.",
      "hash": "092e9f3dc99e23a6fcdf11b38f4af7eee03425bbbf89aeceab8a7b0a69e42aeb"
    },
    {
      "id": "66ce75418fe0c582a644a8746ddf2b175d8c0d1df8ed1fe57305f19571658c74",
      "text": "But what if you want to return multiple objects - an array of objects? What then?",
      "hash": "6372931d11b76c5047f900d2ff8f8509833dae8df6fd4c109533cb00aff2d830"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d77a1ffaa88be679b2426fcf7f8967152dfa00e4298f3ba5da15c5d394c05bc",
      "text": "For instance, you might want your LLM to generate lots of fake data.",
      "hash": "b9d6604384a3650fc832fe301b16979cf35c603560cc7c9e579c5d61f7d28e60"
    },
    {
      "id": "2d2b6d0a8c6437f07ca23ba2e32c6868fed826b55345e8c9c47eff44953de9a3",
      "text": "Scrollycoding",
      "hash": "a92db14e4d481e7975b3459710fbf8ec73dcc232e366b057507f7e2891b1d6da"
    },
    {
      "id": "99b13882f24499668c741b766dc34134cde7a34371a778e5bdbeab6d25613956",
      "text": "Let's first create a Zod schema that we first encountered in our structured outputs example.",
      "hash": "01d099d4e8eab3657f7ef6101a84d1a835740905b7f42f7a1ee8387c509009ef"
    },
    {
      "id": "22cba7d8ec9e1ddd5600dc9af0d89e7eed803b068dab80b5de8925387e1f5353",
      "text": "If you don't understand this I've got a",
      "hash": "5e9d81fcaa76e9791d1452585443539b4096b13d6bd629a10564e18a1a8c1e77"
    },
    {
      "id": "1cf18fae288d4571ef7254ebd97853b083a7422d0e6eceddf132d1e3522f9eb9",
      "text": "free course on Zod",
      "hash": "b5f823d32f4873755cec19afe3637fd627df9013ed43b14d0feb14f844a2e51b"
    },
    {
      "id": "b39cafc89644b7b0547009df1b4c27f5ab008626c3221c1130fbbddf050a03fc",
      "text": "on my sister site Total TypeScript.",
      "hash": "01bbab2f699b69279b5cff10ae3484020d5c171f28efc7a3219f00782b9fc308"
    },
    {
      "id": "e7d97f2681d540199eda5dc52b42c1c06e6d34b243fcb437f96a70c0b25246f0",
      "text": "We should also use descriptions on the schema fields to give the AI more context. Like we've seen before, we can use",
      "hash": "36bb129e8062ea8ac08fd36128e3fca544003f6d8351a7ebd2593fd29574f1ab"
    },
    {
      "id": "387f668b38bf3710f33cd490128a23266b127066112b2c9a8a30ed9a7f3b1378",
      "text": "here.",
      "hash": "dd1d122956efde29d2011224d59be74d13f0c13d18b7c82c66aa0bea294bf720"
    },
    {
      "id": "c977ac09f0a9056d2d5974e5d106aac12b4893350fda4816c38753ff5665680e",
      "text": "Go deeper:",
      "hash": "15ad3d88c6733d9b257c322d3afecc9bce2b18558171007db87598c118ca17f9"
    },
    {
      "id": "c9c27af817d3bf262cb4dc8fffd65469f8ff74306cd4f17507ed2c68c61f55e1",
      "text": "join the waitlist for AI Coding for Real Engineers",
      "hash": "16c3492a8464a0859c944e287a9d433e9a2635f22a6bd8aad59f88c3e80ab732"
    },
    {
      "id": "fac504999fc061993dd6f823aad54560aa35fd3960ce74186a1155b6194b61d6",
      "text": "Then we can pass this schema to the",
      "hash": "623cf0fe4d48fcc203ee705259104fd91e825026f930c06db96d6217d8aa03fc"
    },
    {
      "id": "3ebc7682332b376d32a2fa85ca0e46787cd822606a00db354e6ed73012bd4f6f",
      "text": "function - but we also pass in an output of array.",
      "hash": "60d25acb275103ca7f352c6645b9ca4908f5dfa777f9bfef6b6f0a5f15ea8ef9"
    },
    {
      "id": "bffa22d1954e3423ddadd041e785501be7a4fabe1ad35929c1afc6965f238b6c",
      "text": "Now the object that we get back from",
      "hash": "ac311dc4b64b6b3797317781c7e117c2df5cf336d960da9dcc89e3eff2641ed6"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a5e740de21cd1942850f83176d6facf456a33916e321ed7f0ba16802c5de403",
      "text": "will be this array of users.",
      "hash": "a267c0f2502749b6a0888e011319348657dda42b2c3b53c4a63b4d2c4e1f7df6"
    },
    {
      "id": "934e41e0c65856635589c079bda4fe48b69d273986dead3741922b35bd69c733",
      "text": "What's powerful about this is that we can seed various information about the users, so in this case, they're going to be from the UK like me.",
      "hash": "6660c7bd390d7692637d30bf204eae5c104269b7e6bee05495d3f5c47387768c"
    },
    {
      "id": "d6e2a17429a1a73361e8ffe85ad4982e5e2a4c52a449561d915099244d130382",
      "text": "Let's give this a go. We're going to generate some fake users:",
      "hash": "dc536e0970dba1418ca0f282a2137fb3d77d1d322e28fcedc9be869f7c26bfcf"
    },
    {
      "id": "74b02499fca4b961d83f7882ff9353a14fccbb828dd17e53e38532bdca622638",
      "text": "And just like that, we get our users.",
      "hash": "088b0f11f7051e6f1dfeba52e13b6286d50361caaba82c3c61daefbd8a7fa4e3"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e1d1262cf0eca1aff5346b3f784f746cfafd858175509d105a433a3a6c7ea93",
      "text": "This is particularly cool with",
      "hash": "ffef7bb375f4d6e31fa92ba2425400ad07edf76d646aad96c96a54029b545007"
    },
    {
      "id": "b825ac3536c331e456f334f4c96b6b5c5d885aa8dcdd8d0c0caa9ba8295fff5c",
      "text": "too, where you can stream in the users as they're being created.",
      "hash": "e3c97d1664d935e88ecd93db870d96c14f2df89b4c0d0afb74315f93023f210d"
    },
    {
      "id": "ff9bff16ed12f3fe586a473ac7435cd9f53f34b7a0b62eda03a734626ecfdd5c",
      "text": "So that's how to generate an array of structured objects using the AI SDK.",
      "hash": "daf043d293f8531591cad2d13d19bff0b839160d0904599d8af73f993b1bf676"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a8a1cd1bb5edcd6ada00050c8b520b17120e20f2dfe4313682f9cf8f889aeea",
      "text": "Share on X",
      "hash": "78d21bbf6b047944ec42890d28e151c61dbab35213fc65cc7be70c0c19c24407"
    },
    {
      "id": "52a2a32f29829531a909be41ff5d445fe44e8d97b2ff4f59866662e29f0d0f04",
      "text": "Share on Bluesky",
      "hash": "08863b88a05c60410c38c4caec5bc72535b0f01793ce6cee9171b6358b2c11da"
